    "body": "This gives an effective rank formula for arbitrary quadratic biforms and restricts its two polynomial kernel indices. For a=b=3, the nonzero fifteen-by-fifteen biform block has exactly the ranks {9,12,14,15} over every field. Rank13 is excluded, and universal witnesses attain the four listed values. More generally, for every balanced a=b>=3 quadratic-z family, ranks lie in {a\u00b2,a\u00b2+a,a\u00b2+2a\u22121,a\u00b2+2a}; attainment of all four values is not asserted at larger sizes.\n\nAfter dividing the common coefficient gcd, let D be the largest remaining degree. The indices sum to aD, their first nonzero coefficient-kernel degree recovers both, and the source rank is ab + min(b,mu1) + min(b,mu2). A minimum recurrence vector either has Hankel rank two and degree at least ceil((a-1)D/2), or comes from a rational root of height h and degree (a+1)h. The proof covers zero endpoints, common factors, D=0 and characteristic two.\n\nClaims: AI-QUADRATIC-KERNEL-INDICES-001 and AI-QUADRATIC-INDEX-DICHOTOMY-002, both proof-written-unreviewed. The prior general biform kernel-bundle identity and special-family formulas retain their credit. External inputs: Schoemann\u2013Wiedmann arXiv:1712.03056v1, Theorem2.1; De Teran\u2013Dopico\u2013Mackey MIMS EPrint2013.47 (August22 2013), Theorem6.5. Exact versions, hypotheses and source hashes are in sources.json.\n\nValidation at f00613b:\n- 2,050 complete source-matrix comparisons over Q,F2,F3,F5, including all nonzero F2 triples for a=2,3.\n- 567 positive-degree minimum vectors inspected, with 1,696 direct Hankel kernel-nullity checks including named controls.\n- Universal rank witnesses; the rank15 witness has an exact integer determinant of \u22121 and seven verified unit-determinant blocks.\n- All10 focused tests pass against an immutable export of the committed files and ordinary on-disk report.\n- Repository consistency18 tests, integrated top-coefficient3 tests and integrated paired-window6 tests pass.\n- All five frozen archive replays pass; ten source files verified.\n- Complete local regression suite and current required CI remain pending.\n\nReproduction: python -m unittest discover -s tests -p test_quadratic_kernel_indices.py -v; python -m unittest discover -s tests -v; python tools/replay.py.\n\nThis classifies biform-block ranks in the stated scope, not every full cyclic-tensor slice. No source-space cap, compatible three-leg maps, degeneration, independent mathematical review, formalization or exponent improvement is claimed.",
